"Do not unsubscribe EmptyNetworkManager when not subscribed" (crbug
577403757; no CVE listed yet): Blink's WebRTC EmptyNetworkManager
unsubscribed from the network manager's change notifications on destruction
even when it had never subscribed. The commit doesn't say what that leads
to; it was merged to Stable within a day, so it is carried as a possible
security fix (a one-line guard). chromium/src main commit
dde853af4bf85070c66f88ba822e512494688975 (main@{#1729489}), merged on
2026-10-30 to 158 and to 156 as cacc420d5583a331a68415c203bc1dff14e11bd8
(after the 156.0.8078.84 tag); the 157 merge (Gerrit CL 8687660) was still
open. This is that CL's patch (patch set 7727d2e1abed), the same lines as the 156
merge. Check the merged commit when it lands; drop this once a 157 tag has
it.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/p2p/empty_network_manager.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/p2p/empty_network_manager.cc
index d742aaf..6b316d7 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/p2p/empty_network_manager.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/p2p/empty_network_manager.cc
@@ -30,7 +30,8 @@
 
 EmptyNetworkManager::~EmptyNetworkManager() {
   DCHECK_CALLED_ON_VALID_THREAD(thread_checker_);
-  if (network_manager_for_signaling_thread_) {
+  if (network_manager_for_signaling_thread_ != nullptr &&
+      subscribe_networks_changed_called_) {
     network_manager_for_signaling_thread_->UnsubscribeNetworksChanged(this);
   }
 }
